  "id": "vranje_urban_song",
  "name": "Vranjanska pesma (Vranje urban song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Urban song of Vranje in southern Serbia, formed in the late Ottoman town where Serbian, Turkish and Roma musical life met, and carried into Serbian culture by Bora Stanković's play Koštana, whose songs remain part of the repertoire. A solo singer delivers melismatic love songs of longing (sevdah) to Roma ensembles of violin, clarinet, accordion and tarabuka drum; PGP-RTB recorded the style in the second half of the twentieth century. The toubeleki card stands in for the tarabuka goblet drum.",
  "recipe": "classic Eastern European early-1950s vranjanska pesma, drinking Song, balkan branch. many notes per syllable, solo with instrumental accompaniment. melodic bowed song accompaniment fiddle, clarinet, accordion, toubeleki. treated studio. large-diaphragm condenser, German V72 tube pre, Neve transformer console, LA-2A optical, Neve inductor EQ. tape 15ips plate reverb spring reverb.",
